HST Office on Windows: no App Paths entries for the program names it shares with LibreOffice.

The MSI wrote HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\soffice.exe, swriter.exe,
scalc.exe, simpress.exe, sdraw.exe, smath.exe, sbase.exe and unopkg.exe. Both suites ship programs
with these names, so the one installed last took "Run > soffice" and every ShellExecute of the bare
name, and uninstalling either deleted the entries the other had written. HST Office registers none
of them now; its shortcuts, file types and updater all use the full program path.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/scp2/source/base/registryitem_base.scp
+++ b/scp2/source/base/registryitem_base.scp
@@ -153,21 +153,6 @@
     Styles = ();
 End
 
-RegistryItem gid_Regitem_Software_Microsoft_Windows_Currentversion_Apppaths_Sbase_Exe
-    ParentID = PREDEFINED_HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE;
-    Subkey = "Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\sbase.exe";
-    ModuleID = gid_Module_Prg_Base_Bin;
-    Value = "<progpath>\program\sbase.exe";
-End
-
-RegistryItem gid_Regitem_Software_Microsoft_Windows_Currentversion_Apppaths_Sbase_Exepath
-    ParentID = PREDEFINED_HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE;
-    Subkey = "Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\sbase.exe";
-    ModuleID = gid_Module_Prg_Base_Bin;
-    Name = "Path";
-    Value = "<progpath>";
-End
